 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT authorizing the city of Fulton to discontinue its use of certain waterfront parklands",
    "basePrintNo": "S6756",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S6756-2015",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Oswego County",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6756\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act authorizing the city of Fulton to discontinue\nits use of certain waterfront parklands\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis legislation authorizes the City of Fulton to transfer\napproximately 8.3 acres of city-owned land to the Town of Granby.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1. Authorizes the City of Fulton, through action of its city\ncouncil, to convey waterfront property as described in section 2 of\nthe legislation.\n\nSection 2. Describes the land to be transferred from the City of\nFulton to the Town of Granby as well as the property description for a\nright-of-way easement.\n\nSection 3. States that the land to be transferred be owned and\nmaintained by the Town of Granby as parkland and made available to the\ngeneral public.\n\nSection 4. Establishes that if the property conveyed is ever used for\npurposes other than public parkland, the property shall revert back to\nthe City of Fulton.\n\nSection 5. In the event the Parkland reverts back to the City of\nFulton, the Town of Granby is required to satisfy any federal\nrequirements pertaining to funding prior to conveyance of the\nproperty.\n\nSection 6. This act shall take effect immediately.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nPursuant to a Memorandum of Understanding between the City of Fulton\nand the Town of Granby dated June 11, 2013, regarding annexation of\nlands, the city agrees to transfer 8.3 acres of waterfront property to\nthe Town of Granby for the use of public purposes, such as parkland,\npublic boat launch or other public recreational purposes.\n\nThis legislation was requested by the City of Fulton and the Town of\nGranby. It authorizes the transfer of waterfront property from the\nCity of Fulton to the Town of Granby as well as granting an easement\nof a right-of-way- for ingress and egress.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNone.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the state.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
