    "lawSection": "Oswego County",
    "memo": " BILL NUMBER:  S6756A\n\n TITLE OF BILL :  An act authorizing the city of Fulton to discontinue\nits use of certain waterfront parklands\n\n PURPOSE :\n\nThis legislation authorizes the City of Fulton to transfer\napproximately 8.3 acres of city-owned land to the Town of Granby.\n\n SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS :\n\nSection 1 Authorizes the City of Fulton, through action of its city\ncouncil, to convey waterfront property as described in Section 2 of\nthe legislation to the Town of Granby, provided that the town of\nGranby continue to use the property as parkland, and that the town\nshall continue to provide access to such parkland to the general\npublic.\n\nThe City of Fulton also agrees that the Town of Granby may enact fees\nthat are higher for the residents of the city notwithstanding the\ngeneral prohibition of the enactment of fees which are higher for\nresidents of a municipality conveying the parkland than those fees\ncharges to residents of the municipality receiving the parkland.\n\nThis section further provides that any revenues received by the City\nof Fulton as a result of the conveyance shall be used for capital\nimprovements of existing park and recreational facilities and/or for\nthe acquisition of additional park and recreational facilities.\n\nSection 2 Describes the land to be transferred from the City of Fulton\nto the Town of Granby as well as the property description for a\nright-of-way easement.\n\nSection 3 States that the land to be transferred be owned and\nmaintained by the Town of Granby as parkland and made available to the\ngeneral public.\n\nSection 4 Establishes that if the property conveyed is ever used for\npurposes other than public parkland, the property shall revert back to\nthe City of Fulton.\n\nSection 5 Provides in the event the Parkland reverts back to the City\nof Fulton, the Town of Granby is required to satisfy any federal\nrequirements pertaining to funding prior to conveyance of the\nproperty.\n\nSection 6 Is the effective date.\n\n JUSTIFICATION :\n\nPursuant to a Memorandum of Understanding between the City of Fulton\nand the Town of Granby dated June 11, 2013, regarding annexation of\nlands, the city agrees to transfer 8.3 acres of waterfront property to\nthe Town of Granby for the use of public purposes, such as parkland,\npublic boat launch or other public recreational purposes.\n\nThis legislation was requested by the City of Fulton and the Town of\nGranby. It authorizes the transfer of waterfront property from the\nCity of Fulton to the Town of Granby as well as granting an easement\nof a right-of-way- for ingress and egress.\n\n LEGISLATIVE HISTORY :\n\nNone.\n\n FISCAL IMPLICATIONS :\n\nNone to the state.\n\n EFFECTIVE DATE :\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
